From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Treggat <taggert2222@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 02:05:43 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 19/27] sycl : 9..16-column verify kernels, non-fatal graph
 recording failures

GGML_SYCL_XMX_WIDE=1 (default off) serves 9..16-token batches on XMX:
- q4_K / q6_K register-fed two-tile kernels (bit-identical to the
  joint_matrix two-tile kernels at equal split-K), q6_K and q8_0
  two-tile joint_matrix kernels
- flash attention above 48 query rows as query-row splits (f16 and
  q8_0 KV)
- gated-delta alpha/beta split-K fusion up to 16 columns
1..8-column paths are unchanged.
A sycl::exception raised while a command graph is being recorded is
rethrown to the recorder (the graph then runs eagerly) instead of
exiting the process. GGML_SYCL_LOG_GEMM_FALLBACK and
GGML_SYCL_GRAPH_FAULT_INJECT are diagnostics.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
